	(text "Calibration jumpers used\nto calibrate the transmission\nline to the chamber.\n(Can be done without \npressurizing the chamber.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 56.642 68.072 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "276114cd-fdab-4a53-b1e0-597012e0f859")
	)
	(text "Voltage summing node\nand a jumper to skip\nit for using the DAC\nas an external \ngenerator and testing\nthe DAC alone."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 92.964 67.818 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5c71b1bb-703e-4cca-a186-8671b9c87c4d")
	)
	(text "Theory of\nOperation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.402 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
				(thickness 0.762)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e331856f-8ce7-4a53-8679-7203881337ed")
	)
	(text "CH2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.942 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
				(thickness 0.762)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f2842bc8-b12c-453f-a48f-a4f9833f0549")
	)
	(text_box "The transfer function of the whole system from the Ext_Analog input and DAC outputs to the ADC driver positive output, with the assumption that the internal impedances of the DAC output amplifiers and the external function gen are negligibly small, is given by:\n\nV_+ = (V_1 + V_2) * R_f / (R + 2*R_l), where\n\nV_+ is the positive output of the ADC driver\nV_1 is the output of the opamp connected to the output of the DAC\nV_2 is the external input (Ext_Analog)\nR_f is the feedback resistor of the ADC driver\nR are the values of the summing resistors connected in series with the DAC's opamp output and the external input\nR_l is the resistor between the input of the ADC driver and the node summing the currects from the DAC and the external input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 77.47 0)
		(size 179.07 24.13)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "34ce8218-119c-4eb0-a508-69107c29f70d")
	)
	(text_box "If we set V_- to 0, R_f = R, and R_l = 0, then the voltage measured by the ADC is equal to:\n\nV_o = V_1 + V_2\ncreating a perfect summing amplifier.\n\nThe value of 1kΩ was chosen for the resistor R and capacitors were added in parallel with it to create a low pass filter with cutoff of 1.6MHz. A filter with the same cutoff frequency was reproduced after the DAC driver to create a sharper cutoff."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 104.14 0)
		(size 72.39 29.21)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "553641b4-a688-4076-8daf-4da23916d672")
	)
